@startuml feature_v0.7.0_F-008_sequence
' Runtime truth for F-008 v0.7.0 — Export and Interchange
' Reversed from code at commit 92c2578a. Cast is the participants: list of feature_v0.7.0_F-008_front-matter.yaml, name for name.
title F-008 v0.7.0 — Export and Interchange
autonumber

actor "Analyst" as Analyst
participant "routes.export_import" as ExportApi
participant "export.registry" as Registry
participant "JsonExporter" as Json
participant "RdfExporter" as Rdf
participant "GraphSession" as Session

group F-008-US1 — export a graph into the format my downstream tool reads
  Analyst -> ExportApi : POST /api/export, ExportRequest
  activate ExportApi
  ExportApi -> Registry : resolve exporter by format
  Registry --> ExportApi : exporter instance
  ExportApi -> Session : read ContextNode and ContextEdge
  Session --> ExportApi : graph data
  ExportApi -> Rdf : serialise
  activate Rdf
  Rdf --> ExportApi : serialised document
  deactivate Rdf
  ExportApi --> Analyst : export payload
  deactivate ExportApi
  Analyst -> ExportApi : POST /api/export/distance-enriched, DistanceExportRequest
  ExportApi --> Analyst : export payload with pairwise distances
end

group F-008-US2 — read an exported graph with a default-graph reader and still see its provenance
  Analyst -> ExportApi : POST /api/export naming a graph
  activate ExportApi
  ExportApi -> Json : serialise into a caller-named graph
  activate Json
  Json -> Json : keep the caller's graph name for the caller's statements (semantica/export/json_exporter.py:514)
  Json -> Json : write our own statements to the default graph
  Json --> ExportApi : document
  deactivate Json
  ExportApi --> Analyst : default-graph reader still sees provenance
  deactivate ExportApi
end

group failure — caller-named graph would capture the serializer's own statements
  Json -> Json : write own statements outside the named graph
  Json --> ExportApi : document a default-graph reader can read
end

group failure — graph-level metadata has no subject to attach to
  Rdf -> Rdf : no document node has ever been minted (semantica/export/rdf_exporter.py:920)
  Rdf --> ExportApi : metadata omitted rather than attached to an invented subject
end

group failure — import file cannot be read and reports the failure in its response
  Analyst -> ExportApi : POST /api/import
  ExportApi --> Analyst : ImportResponse carrying the failure
end

note over Json
  invariants: DOM-008-R1, DOM-008-R2
  open: issue #1147 supplies the default metadata subject once it lands (semantica/export/rdf_exporter.py:920)
  timeout: none documented - retry: none documented - idempotency: none documented
end note

@enduml
